  <packagedElement xmi:type="uml:Stereotype" xmi:id="_RKln-z0aEe6hwoNCJlhprA" name="dController">
    <ownedComment xmi:id="_RKln_D0aEe6hwoNCJlhprA">
      <body>The Controller defines application behavior and the Business Logic involving more than one ModelClass. It dispatches requests and selects views for presentation. It interprets user inputs and maps them into actions.
Controller, with Views and Associations define the application flow. A controller represents the Business logic where a certain flow is physically implemented.
In a Service Oriented Architecture (SOA) a Controller can be exposed by a Physical Service.</body>
    </ownedComment>
    <ownedAttribute xmi:id="_RKln_T0aEe6hwoNCJlhprA" name="base_Class" association="_RKmLmT0aEe6hwoNCJlhprA">
      <type xmi:type="uml:Class" href="pathmap://UML_METAMODELS/UML.metamodel.uml#Class"/>
    </ownedAttribute>
  </packagedElement>
  <packagedElement xmi:type="uml:Stereotype" xmi:id="_RKln_j0aEe6hwoNCJlhprA" name="dDataEntity">
    <ownedComment xmi:id="_RKln_z0aEe6hwoNCJlhprA">
      <body>An encapsulation of data that is recognized by a business domain expert as a thing. Logical data entities can be tied to applications, repositories, and services and may be structured according to implementation considerations.</body>
    </ownedComment>
    <ownedAttribute xmi:id="_RKloAD0aEe6hwoNCJlhprA" name="PrivacyClassification">
